# Windows batch files: keep the bytes exactly as committed.
#
# cmd.exe reads a .bat with the console codepage, which on Korean Windows
# is CP949 - not UTF-8. Saving Korean text as UTF-8 and switching with
# "chcp 65001" inside the file does not fix it: cmd changes codepage
# mid-parse and then resumes reading at a byte offset that no longer lines
# up, chopping commands in half. So the Korean-language .bat files here
# are stored in CP949 with CRLF endings, and git must not "helpfully"
# normalize either one.
*.bat -text
